From 4cded138238db6b3ba8bf208fa3b39f200f7067d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Masahiro Ide <imasahiro9@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Apr 2014 16:36:44 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] bug fixed that introduced at 800f8fb716694


diff --git a/java/src/libbun/parser/ast/ZNode.java b/java/src/libbun/parser/ast/ZNode.java
index 9b71d71..54c0c73 100644
--- a/java/src/libbun/parser/ast/ZNode.java
+++ b/java/src/libbun/parser/ast/ZNode.java
@@ -51,7 +51,7 @@ public abstract class ZNode {

 	public ZNode(ZNode ParentNode, ZToken SourceToken, int Size) {
 		assert(this != ParentNode);
-		ParentNode.SetChild(this, ZNode._EnforcedParent);
+		this.ParentNode = ParentNode;
 		this.SourceToken = SourceToken;
 		if(Size > 0) {
 			this.AST = LibZen._NewNodeArray(Size);
-- 
2.25.1

        You will be given the root cause of a bug, the commit message and the corresponding patch.
        You need to extract all code statements that lead to the bug from the patch, based on the root cause and the commit message.

        Root cause:
        The bug was likely caused by the incorrect handling of the parent-child relationship in the `ZNode` class. The previous implementation used a method (`SetChild`) to set the parent node, which may not have correctly established the relationship or could have led to unintended side effects. By directly assigning the parent node to the instance variable, the code ensures that the parent-child relationship is accurately represented without relying on potentially flawed method logic.

        Commit message:
        bug fixed that introduced at 800f8fb716694  

        Patch:

 	public ZNode(ZNode ParentNode, ZToken SourceToken, int Size) {
 		assert(this != ParentNode);
-		ParentNode.SetChild(this, ZNode._EnforcedParent);
+		this.ParentNode = ParentNode;
 		this.SourceToken = SourceToken;
 		if(Size > 0) {
 			this.AST = LibZen._NewNodeArray(Size);
 		}
 		else {
 			this.AST = null;
 		}
 	}



        Provide a response strictly in the following format:
        Code statements:
        <text1>
        <text2>
        ...
        <textN>
